\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {I.2}{\ignorespaces The "Keeling Curve": this graph illustrates the evolution of atmospheric \ce {CO2} concentration over the last two thousand years. Named after Charles D. Keeling who initiated the measurement project of continuous \ce {CO2} measurement at Mauna Loa observatory (Hawaii, U.S.) in 1958 \citep {keeling_atmospheric_2017}, the data is completed by ice core measurements \citep {rubino_revised_2019}. The industrial revolution is clearly highlighted by the dramatic increase that started in the late 18{th} century. Data can be found here: \url  {https://keelingcurve.ucsd.edu/}.}}{10}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:keeling_curve}{{I.2}{10}{The "Keeling Curve": this graph illustrates the evolution of atmospheric \ce {CO2} concentration over the last two thousand years. Named after Charles D. Keeling who initiated the measurement project of continuous \ce {CO2} measurement at Mauna Loa observatory (Hawaii, U.S.) in 1958 \citep {keeling_atmospheric_2017}, the data is completed by ice core measurements \citep {rubino_revised_2019}. The industrial revolution is clearly highlighted by the dramatic increase that started in the late 18\up {th} century. Data can be found here: \url {https://keelingcurve.ucsd.edu/}}{figure.caption.5}{}}
